Alembic migrations for Milsurp Monitor.

Apply everything outstanding:      make migrate
Generate a new revision:           make migration m="add widget table"
Show the current revision:         .venv/bin/alembic -c backend/alembic.ini current
Show the history:                  .venv/bin/alembic -c backend/alembic.ini history

Every migration in this directory is written to be idempotent: it inspects the
database before creating or dropping anything, so re-running it against a
database that already has the change is a no-op rather than an error. That
matters because the application also calls create_all() at startup for fresh
checkouts, so a table can legitimately exist before its migration runs.

The database URL is not configured here -- env.py reads it from the application
config file, so migrations always follow database.path for the current mode.
